{
  "purpose": "Opposite-facing portraits so two dialogue figures can face each other (left slot looks right, right slot looks left).",
  "date": "2026-10-05",
  "method": "Lossless horizontal pixel mirror (PIL Image.transpose FLIP_LEFT_RIGHT, PNG saved with optimize). No generation model and no other postprocessing; alpha is kept exactly.",
  "verification": "For every file, flipping the saved mirror back reproduced every RGBA pixel of the base art (checked in full, not sampled). Unity test NpcPortraitFacingTests samples the same property from the shipped files.",
  "facingMeasurement": "Base-art direction from the macOS Vision face-landmark nose offset: (nose centroid x - face-contour centre x) / contour half-width, in image space. Positive means the nose sits right of the face centre, so the face looks toward the viewer's right. Mirrored copies gave the same magnitude with the opposite sign (checked for mark-kus, hero-warrior, jean-jorin). Vision's coarse yaw value was not used.",
  "limits": [
    "Pyonya (+0.233) and Jean (-0.209) are close to frontal, so their direction is the least certain.",
    "The measurement is head direction; torso direction was only checked by eye.",
    "Mirroring flips asymmetric details (handedness, scars, hair parting) and the light direction."
  ],
  "provenance": "candidate_model_unknown (the base art is built-in image_gen output; the mirrors add no model)",
  "productionApproved": false,
